 <subsection xml:id="ticket-sales">
  <title>Event Ticket Sales</title>
<p>
Imagine you are organizing a charity E-sports Tournament. Before the big day, student tickets are sold, and their prices vary depending on factors like early-bird discounts or VIP tier additions.
</p><p>
To help the event planning committee budget properly, you will write a Python program that collects all ticket sale prices into a list and runs analysis functions to calculate key metrics, such as total revenue, average ticket sales, and other ticket statistics.
</p><p>
There are four types of tickets with different prices:
</p>
<p>
<ul>
<li>$10 (Early-Bird Student Ticket)</li>
<li>$15 (Standard General Admission)</li>
<li>$25 (VIP Pass with Merch)</li>
<li>$40 (Front-Row Tournament Pass)</li>
</ul>
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Program Requirements</strong>
</p>

<p>
<ul>
<li><p>Calculate Total Revenue</p>
    <p>
        <ul>
            <li><p>Function: <c>calculate_total(prices)</c></p></li>
            <li><p>Input: A list of prices.</p></li>
            <li><p>Processing: Iterate through the list using a loop to sum all values.</p></li>
            <li><p>Return: The total result of all ticket sales.</p></li>
        </ul>
    </p>
</li>
<li><p>Calculate Average Ticket Price</p>
    <p>
        <ul>
            <li><p>Function: <c>calculate_average(prices)</c></p></li>
            <li><p>Input: A list of prices.</p></li>
            <li><p>Input check: If the list is empty, return -1.</p></li>
            <li><p>Processing: Iterate through the list using a loop to find the average price.</p></li>
            <li><p>Return: The average price of all ticket sales.</p></li>
        </ul>
    </p>
</li>
<li><p>Find Maximum Ticket Prices</p>
    <p>
        <ul>
            <li><p>Function: <c>find_max_price(prices)</c></p></li>
            <li><p>Input: A list of prices.</p></li>
            <li><p>Processing: Iterate through the list using a loop to find the maximum price.</p></li>
            <li><p>Return: The maximum price of all ticket sales.</p></li>
        </ul>
    </p>

</li>
<li><p>Find Minimum Ticket Prices</p>
    <p>
        <ul>
            <li><p>Function: <c>find_min_price(prices)</c></p></li>
            <li><p>Input: A list of prices.</p></li>
            <li><p>Processing: Iterate through the list using a loop to find the minimum price.</p></li>
            <li><p>Return: The minimum price of all ticket sales.</p></li>
        </ul>
    </p>

</li>
<li><p>Count Tickets</p>
    <p>
        <ul>
            <li><p>Function: <c>count_tickets(prices, target_price)</c></p></li>
            <li><p>Input: A list of prices and a target price.</p></li>
            <li><p>Processing: Iterate through the list using a loop to count how many tickets are priced at the target price.</p></li>
            <li><p>Print: The number of tickets priced at the target price.</p></li>
        </ul>
    </p>

</li>
<li><p>Main Program Flow (Outside Functions)</p>
    <p>
        <ul>
            <li><p>Create ticket_prices as an empty list</p></li>
            <li><p>Collect User Input (Populate the List)</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><p>Loop until the user enters -1 to stop.</p></li>
                    <li><p>Ask the user to enter ticket prices one by one.</p></li>
                    <li><p>If the input is not -1, add input to the ticket_prices list.</p></li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><p>Call each function with the ticket_prices list</p></li>
            <li><p>Display a clean, formatted summary showing:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><p>Total Revenue</p></li>
                    <li><p>Average Ticket Price</p></li>
                    <li><p>Maximum Ticket Price</p></li>
                    <li><p>Minimum Ticket Price</p></li>
                    <li><p>Count of Each Ticket Type</p></li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </p>
</li>
</ul>
</p>

<p>
    Sample Output:
</p>
<pre>
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): 10
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): 15
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): 25
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): 40
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): 10
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): 15
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): 10
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): 40
Enter a ticket price (or enter -1 to finish): -1
Total revenue generated: $ 165.00
Average ticket price: $ 20.62
Highest ticket price sold: $ 40.00
Lowest ticket price sold: $ 10.00
Number of tickets sold at $ 10.00 :  3
Number of tickets sold at $ 15.00 :  2
Number of tickets sold at $ 25.00 :  1
Number of tickets sold at $ 40.00 :  2
</pre>

